@startuml Asset Tagging Flow - Simplified
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam BoxPadding 20

title Asset Registry Tagging - Simplified Flow

box "Tag Definition" #LightBlue
  actor Engineer
  participant "PR Review" as PR
end box

box "Tag Management" #LightGreen
  actor "Ops/Admin" as Admin
  participant "Retool UI" as Retool
  participant "Asset Registry\nService" as Service
  database "asset_tag\nTable" as TagDB
end box

box "Client Services" #LightPink
  participant "AssetTypes\nClient (10s)" as Client
  database "Tags Cache" as Cache
  participant "Services" as Services
end box

== 1. Tag Definition (One-time) ==

Engineer -> PR: Create new tag definition\n(REBASING, STABLE, etc.)
note right
  Tag must have:
  - Name (e.g., "REBASING")
  - Description
  - Behavioral implications
end note
PR --> Engineer: Merged & deployed ✓

== 2. Apply Tags to Assets ==

Admin -> Retool: Select asset tags
Retool -> Service: SetAssetTags gRPC\n(assetTypeID, tags[])
Service -> TagDB: Insert asset_tag records\n(asset_id, tag)
note right
  Unique constraint on
  (asset_id, tag) pair

  Audit trail via entaudit
end note
TagDB --> Service: Tags stored ✓
Service --> Retool: Return current tags
Retool --> Admin: Success confirmation

== 3. Client Cache Population ==

Client -> Service: ListTagsWithAssetTypeIDs gRPC\n(every 10s)
activate Client
activate Service
Service -> TagDB: Query all asset_tag records
TagDB --> Service: Return tag -> assetIDs map
Service --> Client: Map[tag][]assetTypeIDs
deactivate Service

Client -> Cache: Update tagsCache\n(sync.Map)
note right
  Cache structure:
  tagsCache[tag] = []assetTypeIDs

  Example:
  tagsCache["REBASING"] =
    ["ethereum:steth", "ethereum:reth"]
end note
Cache --> Client: Tags cached ✓
deactivate Client

== 4. Service Usage ==

Services -> Client: GetByTags("REBASING")
activate Services
activate Client
Client -> Cache: Lookup tag in tagsCache
Cache --> Client: Return []assetTypeIDs
Client --> Services: List of rebasing assets
deactivate Client
deactivate Services

@enduml
